umpy, also problematic. Candidate D has arrogance and weak leadership, also problematic. Candidate A has leadership but unorganized and poor at criticism. Which is best overall? Might be Candidate A: strong leadership, anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, but concerns about criticism and organization. Could be mitigated. I'd argue for Candidate A as provisional.\n\nThus public message: I propose Candidate A, citing strengths and concerns, and note need to discuss others.\n\nProceed."}
